  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political atmosphere in Indonesia has intensified following reports that Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka expressed an intention to resign to President Prabowo Subianto. This move coincides with public scrutiny and demonstrations concerning the authenticity of the Vice President's educational credentials. In response to the rumors, Gibran indicated that he received counsel from the President to remain committed to resolving the issue through the legal system. Meanwhile, political figures and government officials have clarified the constitutional procedures for such a resignation, noting that the legislative body, rather than the executive office, maintains the authority to oversee the process. As the situation develops, various political parties are monitoring the legal implications, even as public demonstrations near government buildings have begun to subside. The ongoing situation remains a point of significant national interest as stakeholders await further clarity on the Vice President's official status.",
